  "chapter": {
    "number": 139,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(140) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Rescue me, O Lord, from the evil man; deliver me from the unjust man.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who have devised injustice in their hearts; all the day they prepared war.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have sharpened their tongue as the tongue of a serpent; the poison of asps is under their lips. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Keep me, O Lord, from the hand of the sinner; rescue me from unjust men; who have purposed to overthrow my goings.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The proud have hid a snare for me, and have stretched out ropes for snares for my feet; they set a stumbling block for me near the path. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I said to the Lord, You are my God; listen, O Lord, to the voice of my supplication.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord God, the strength of my salvation; you have screened my head in the day of battle.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me not, O Lord, to the sinner,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 250
          },
          {
            "text": "according to my desire: they have devised mischief against me; forsake me not, lest they should be exalted. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "As for the head of them that compass me, the mischief of their lips shall cover them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Coals of fire shall fall upon them on the earth; and you shall cast them down in afflictions: they shall not bear up under them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A talkative man shall not prosper on the earth: evils shall hunt the unrighteous man to destruction.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I know that the Lord will maintain the cause of the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 251
          },
          {
            "text": "poor, and the right of the needy ones.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Surely the righteous shall give thanks to your name: the upright shall dwell in your presence.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
